// Copilot CLI settings (~/.copilot/config.json). The CLI writes its own state
// here too (firstLaunchAt, ...) and merges rather than replaces, so a baked
// value survives. Its own header calls the file automatically managed and
// points at settings.json for user settings — but the folder-trust check is
// read from THIS file, verified on the CLI 1.0.73 image: trustedFolders in
// settings.json is migrated here only after the check has already fired.
//
// Without it, every first session opens on a blocking "Do you trust the files
// in this folder?" dialog, which --allow-all-tools/-paths/-urls do NOT cover:
// a fresh workspace would sit on that prompt inside tmux instead of on the
// agent prompt. /workspace is the container's clone of the repo — exactly what
// the workspace exists to work on.
{
  "trustedFolders": ["/workspace"]
}
